<$TOP/mkfiles/mkfile.proto
<$TOP/BOOT/mkfiles/hostflags/$cputype/mkfile

# the host bootstrap compiler: builds goken's own C sources (compilers/,
# assemblers/, linkers/, lib_core/, ...) using gcc, so that the goken
# cross-tools (5c/6c/7c/8c/...) exist in the first place.
#
# the --std=gnu89 is needed because recent gcc have too many warnings
# by default that prevent compiling goken, and -Wno-cpp is to avoid
# certain errors; $CFLAGS_ARCH (from BOOT/mkfiles/hostflags/$cputype/mkfile)
# adds any flags needed for this specific host CPU.
#
# claude: this include was missing its "BOOT/" prefix -- mkfiles/hostflags/
# (without BOOT/) has never existed, only BOOT/mkfiles/hostflags/ does, so
# mk silently skipped it ("warning: skipping missing include file") and
# $CFLAGS_ARCH was always empty here. Concretely this meant
# BOOT/mkfiles/hostflags/arm64/mkfile's `CFLAGS_ARCH=-fsigned-char` (needed
# because plain `char` defaults to unsigned on arm64, unlike x86 -- see
# that file's own comment and compilers/8ck/mul.c's pre-existing note on
# the same issue) never actually reached gcc, so 6c/8c/8ck -- themselves
# built BY this boot-gcc step -- inherited an unsigned `char`, silently
# breaking their own mul.c (constant-multiply strength reduction, "bad
# mul alg" on lib_core/libc/math/lrand.c's `A*lo - R*hi`, see
# docs/claude_notes/notes_libc_selfhost.txt) whenever built on an arm64
# host. Found while chasing exactly that failure; fixed here at the root
# (the missing path prefix) rather than by touching mul.c itself, since
# -fsigned-char was already the codebase's own recorded intended fix.
#
# once the cross-tools can compile lib_core/libc themselves, a later
# 'mk objtype=$cputype' build (see mkfiles/$cputype/mkfile) can use them
# as CC/AS/LD instead of gcc, to self-host goken with goken.
#
#TODO was -O2 but better -O0 for ease of debugging with gdb
#note: SANITIZE is optionally set by ./configure --asan
#coupling: scripts/build-mk.sh CFLAGS
CFLAGS=-O0 -fno-inline -ggdb $SANITIZE -I$TOP/BOOT/include $CFLAGS_COMMON
CC=gcc -c --std=gnu89 -Wno-cpp $CFLAGS_ARCH
#alt: could use ld?
LD=gcc
#alt: could use gas?
AS=gcc
O=o
# the system's own binutils ar: mkfiles/mksyslib/mklib use $AR (not
# goken's own iar, used by mkfiles/$cputype/mkfile) since a
# gcc/clang-produced library is only ever linked by the host's own
# linker, never by goken's own Xl
AR=ar
